// Verus program: minimum moves to transform a -> b
// Operation rules:
// - + (any positive odd)
// - - (any positive even)
//
// Key logic (well-known parity reasoning):
// Let d = b - a.
// - If d == 0: 0 moves.
// - If d > 0 (need to increase):
//     * If d is odd: 1 move (add exactly d, which is a positive odd).
//     * If d is even: 2 moves (add an odd to flip parity, then add another odd).
// - If d < 0 (need to decrease):
